today i want to take a few minutes to  tell you about a really interesting tech  project called ethernet cloud we  partnered with ethernet cloud to create  this video so they support the david  pakman show help make the show possible  and we thank them for that it's been a  fascinating project to learn more about  so let's just dive right in ethernet  cloud is a decentralized confidential  computing platform on an ethereum  compatible blockchain what does that  mean  confidential computing is a pretty new  cloud computing technology takes an ar  an organization's most sensitive data  isolates it in a protected cpu while  it's being processed where stronger  end-to-end data security is provided  through exclusive control of the  encryption keys the data being processed  is only accessible to authorized  programming code it's invisible to  anyone else including whoever is  providing the cloud  ethernet cloud says that they've  developed  a  cloud computing  built specially for privacy anonymity  and availability they say their vision  about the future of cloud computing has  three important features it's encrypted  it's anonymous and it's continuously  available  and the fact that they're using  blockchain technology is a big part of  this it allows for a decentralized  ecosystem  where regular cloud software  runs as decentralized cloud app so  inside of ethernet cloud the nodes of  the blockchain are location agnostic  self-replicating and always spawning  around the internet without user  interaction this is the advantage of  combining cloud computing with  blockchain technology the  decentralization aspect is very cool  because they avoid the middleman that  you would normally have with centralized  cloud computing which ethernet cloud  says allows them to provide a more  trustless cost-effective and reliable  solution that does a better job of  empowering everyday users and users can  monetize their idle computing resources  join  public fog computing infrastructure and  then when you look at the privacy  advantages authority cloud says that by  providing encryption on all levels user  data is protected when it's at rest in  transit and during use or during  processing using this trustless model  the software enforces private uh privacy  security controls that provide peace of  mind to the owners of the data now with  regard to anonymity  when data is in a decentralized  environment like this  the anonymity is the key element that  ensures the right privacy levels  ethernet cloud says they have a special  understanding of the demand for  anonymity when running cloud computing  applications so it's one of the biggest  focuses or foci of what they do and then  finally the availability of the data  availability can be a challenge with  decentralized cloud storage and  processing models like this but that's  another problem that ethernet cloud  wants to solve they are adapting and  developing decentralized apps that run  seamlessly but also provide  uninterrupted availability one other  aspect of the technology i want to cover  is what's referred to as ethernet  cloud's proof of execution this is the  method by which computational tasks are  run in a decentralized way while the  tasks run  various metadata information is being  stored on the blockchain and the actual  data is transferred using the ipfs  protocol so using this method  computational tasks are certified on the  blockchain while at the same time  improving availability abil the ability  of the research to be reproduced  ethernet cloud is headed up by founder  and ceo joseph peterfie  who actually has over 20 years of  experience filling cornerstone tech  infrastructure roles at the usdod  the max planck digital library really  fascinating projects ethernet cloud had  a very successful pre-sale they've had a  ton of community support from the start  the public sale is scheduled for q3 this  year until that happens they have a  registration form where people can sign  up ahead of time ethernet cloud has  become a member of the confidential  computing consortium that's a community  focused on projects  for securing data and accelerating the  adoption of confidential computing  through open collaboration the ccc has a  really cool ethos if you read about them  on the website i think it says a lot  about ethernet cloud being a member i've  really enjoyed learning about ethernet  crowd while making a ethernet cloud  while making the video take a minute to  check out their website look at the  white paper check out the road map the  team is interesting read more about them  you can follow ethernet cloud on social  they're on twitter telegram discord  reddit they do a really good job job of  keeping the community updated  and the link to the ethernet cloud  website is underneath the video  thank you to ethernet cloud for  partnering with us on this video and as  i always make sure to say in every  partnered video we do  nothing in this video is financial  advice of any kind
 

